{
  "body_human_readable": "### Oklahoma City Thunder Crowned 2024-2025 NBA Champions\n\nThe Oklahoma City Thunder have secured the 2024-2025 NBA championship, defeating the Indiana Pacers in a hard-fought seven-game series. This marks a significant achievement for the young Thunder team, capping off a dominant season.\n\nThe Thunder's victory was the culmination of a season where they consistently performed as a top team, finishing with the best record in the league at 68-14. Their impressive run through the playoffs concluded with a 4-3 series win over the Pacers.\n\nShai Gilgeous-Alexander led the charge for the Thunder and was named the Most Valuable Player for the season. He was also the league's leading scorer, averaging 32.7 points per game.\n\nOther standout performers during the 2024-2025 season included Domantas Sabonis of the Sacramento Kings, who led the league in rebounds, and Trae Young of the Atlanta Hawks, who was the assists leader. The Rookie of the Year was awarded to Stephon Castle of the San Antonio Spurs.\n\nThe Thunder's championship run was highlighted by their statistical dominance throughout the regular season and playoffs. Their performance has led to discussions about the potential for a new dynasty in the NBA.",
